NeoSCAD patch to manifold-rust 0.13.1 (crates.io): collapse_edge refuses a
collapse that would move any surrounding triangle out of its own plane.
Without it, simplify_topology can slide a vertex across a crease between
faces that carry no face IDs (or whose references dedupe_edge copied from
a neighbour) and change the solid: a BOSL2 cubetruss union gained a
7.31 mm^3 notch. Regression test: crates/geom/tests/collapse_crease.rs.

Upstream: not reported. C++ Manifold 3.5.2 gives the same wrong result;
Manifold's master has rewritten CollapseEdge (untested there).

Apply from the crate root after deleting the paths listed in `removed`:
patch -p1 < this file. The crate's sources use CRLF line endings.
See vendor/README.md ("The edge-collapse bug").

--- a/src/edge_op.rs
+++ b/src/edge_op.rs
